.TH "APP" "1" "2026-11-28" "app v1.2.3"
.SH "NAME"
app \- copy files between hosts
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
\fBapp\fR [flags] [command] [args]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
App copies files.
.PP
It reads its config from FILE.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR FILE
the config file (default: $HOME/.apprc)
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-debug\fR, \fB\-\-trace\fR
write debug output
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR string
the output format (default: json) (allowed: json, yaml)
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR string
the token
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show help, then exit
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "app get"
.PP
get a file
.PP
\fBapp get\fR [flags] [command] path [dest]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-retries\fR int
the number of retries (default: 3)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
overwrite a file (required)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show help, then exit
.PP
\fBArguments:\fR
.TP
\fIpath\fR
the path of the file
.TP
\fIdest\fR
where to write the file (default: .)
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
  app get a.txt
.fi
.RE
.SS "app get all"
.PP
get each file
.PP
\fBapp get all\fR [flags] [args]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
write what it gets, and get nothing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show help, then exit
.SS "app help"
.PP
show help for any command
.PP
\fBapp help\fR [flags] [args]
.PP
Help provides help for any app command.
.PP
Simply type app help [path to command] for full details.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show help, then exit
.SS "app put"
.PP
put a file
.PP
\fBapp put\fR [flags] [args]
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show help, then exit
.SS "app version"
.PP
show app version information
.PP
\fBapp version\fR [flags] [args]
.PP
Show app version information.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
show help, then exit
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
  app \-\-config x.yaml get a.txt
  app get \-r 5 a.txt /tmp
.fi
.RE
.SH "NOTES"
.PP
See https://example.com/app for more.
